        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1e8091d8-0177-54ff-8c52-0d18ca55ceb1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Robert Sikoryak, Samuel Beckett, Daria Morgendorffer\n- Projects: Masterpiece Comics, Carousel\n- Works: Waiting for Godot, Crime and Punishment, Dostoyevsky Comics, Waiting to Go, Beavis and Butt-Head, Daria\n- Topics: comic adaptations, multimedia comics slide shows\n\nFacts:\n- Robert Sikoryak, born in 1964, is an American artist whose work is usually signed R. Sikoryak.\n- Robert Sikoryak specializes in making comic adaptations of literary classics.\n- Since 1997, Carousel has been a long-running multimedia comics slide show hosted by cartoonist Robert Sikoryak and presented in venues across the United States and Canada.\n- Under the series title Masterpiece Comics, Robert Sikoryak created Crime and Punishment in the style of Bob Kane-era Batman as Dostoyevsky Comics starring Raskol.\n- Under Masterpiece Comics, Robert Sikoryak also mixed Waiting for Godot with Beavis and Butt-Head to create Waiting to Go.\n- Waiting for Godot is a play by Samuel Beckett in which Vladimir and Estragon wait for someone named Godot, who never arrives, while they converse and encounter three other characters.\n- Daria Morgendorffer is a fictional character from MTV's animated series Beavis and Butt-Head and its spin-off Daria.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "49fc7943-f891-58c8-94f0-c6a0e247e234",
        "text": "Page: Robert Sikoryak. Sentence: Robert Sikoryak (born 1964) is an American artist whose work is usually signed R. Sikoryak.\nPage: Robert Sikoryak. Sentence: He specializes in making comic adaptations of literature classics.\nPage: Robert Sikoryak. Sentence: Under the series title \"Masterpiece Comics\", these include \"Crime and Punishment\" rendered in Bob Kane–era Batman style, becoming \"Dostoyevsky Comics\", starring Raskol; and \"Waiting for Godot\" mixed with \"Beavis and Butt-Head\", becoming \"Waiting to Go\".\nPage: Waiting for Godot. Sentence: Waiting for Godot ( ) is a play by Samuel Beckett, in which two characters, Vladimir and Estragon, wait for the arrival of someone named Godot who never arrives, and while waiting they engage in a variety of discussions and encounter three other characters.\nPage: Carousel (comics). Sentence: Carousel is a long-running multimedia comics slide show hosted by cartoonist Robert Sikoryak (\"Masterpiece Comics\") that has been presented in various venues in the United States and Canada since 1997.\nPage: Daria Morgendorffer. Sentence: Daria Morgendorffer is a fictional character from MTV's animated series \"Beavis and Butt-Head\" and its spin-off \"Daria\".",
